Cause: the CEF development app and five helper templates duplicated the historical 0.9.6 value, so macOS crash reports ignored the current 1.1.3 project version. Decision: tauri.conf.json is the bundle-version authority. prepare-cef stamps helpers before signing; run-cef-dev-app stamps the main app before signing; ensure-cef-dev-runtime invalidates cached helpers when either the authority or stamping logic changes. Templates carry only 0.0.0 and invalid versions fail before compilation. Tests execute the real scripts, inspect both bundle version keys, and cover cache refresh.
